WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:09.708
- [Narrator] JaQuel Knight
is the creative mind

00:00:09.708 --> 00:00:12.720
many of Beyoncé's iconic performances.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.700
He's worked with her for years

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.220
and he's been dancing his entire life.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.320
- I remember dancing in my
grandmother's living room

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.210
at the age of four and five,

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:23.880
copying the things I saw on TV.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.070
As I got older I remember copying all the

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.950
major iconic MTV award shows,

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.760
performances, Soul Train performances.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.260
And then when I was 16

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.720
I started my own dance group

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.460
with my best friend in Atlanta

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.560
and that was kind of
the first serious step

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.240
towards choreography
and creative direction.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.590
- [Narrator] At just 18,

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:48.620
JaQuel landed a gig choreographing

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.703
- One of the best videos of all time.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:54.910
- [Narrator] Single Ladies.

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:56.390
- [JaQuel] Frank Gatson Junior,

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:58.660
who was choreographer
and creative director

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:01.760
for Beyoncé and Destiny's Child for,

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.310
you know, ages.

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:07.240
He was actually working on
Michelle Williams' debut project.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:08.657
In the process of that he was like,

00:01:08.657 --> 00:01:10.420
"Wow, you know how to teach,

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:11.580
you know how to deal with people,

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:12.930
you lead really well,

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.760
you know, how bout you
come on board and help

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.050
choreograph the video with us."

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:16.883
And the next week he was like,

00:01:16.883 --> 00:01:19.410
"Can you come choreograph
the entire promo tour?"

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.120
And then a few months went by,

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:21.953
he called and was like,

00:01:21.953 --> 00:01:23.810
"Yo, I have this Beyoncé record,

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.580
can you fly to New York tonight?"

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.560
I was like, "Yo, I just got the call!

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:30.534
Going to New York tonight! Yoncé!"

00:01:30.534 --> 00:01:31.367
(laughs)

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:32.260
Got to New York,

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:33.830
the record was Single Ladies.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:35.793
Once getting in the space with her,

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:37.880
starting to dance with her,

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.650
and see how she thinks and move

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:41.330
through the project and how she

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:42.900
see things in her head,

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.690
I was completely blown away.

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:45.940
- [Narrator] Ten years later,

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:47.270
JaQuel and Beyoncé teamed up

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:49.620
for yet another iconic performance.

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.350
They incorporated homecoming
moves made popular by

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.270
Historically Black
Colleges and Universities.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:57.120
- [JaQuel] You know, that
was a thing that Beyoncé

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.097
kinda woke up with one day and was like,

00:01:59.097 --> 00:02:02.400
"Yo, let's do this homecoming experience."

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.670
The research behind it,

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:06.810
we went back and watched football games.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.836
You watch homecomings,

00:02:08.836 --> 00:02:10.460
so many probates.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:13.200
We watched fraternities in the club,

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.280
we watched sororities.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.660
We watched a load of just
black college experiences

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.100
and then kind of got in the mindset

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.000
of creating the right energy.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.240
I wish I could count the hours

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.850
that went into it but we worked

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.950
for like five to six months on it.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:34.430
Working with B during the
rehearsal process is like,

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.830
it's kind of a out of body experience.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:40.880
People don't understand
the amount of effort.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.760
Her work ethic is out of this world.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.750
And it's never just one thing.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.340
When we're creating choreography it's

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.348
okay boom, where's wardrobe at?

00:02:49.348 --> 00:02:50.720
Bring them in so they can see

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:51.950
what the choreography is.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:52.970
Okay, boom.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.280
Where are we on the stage?

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:55.590
Let's make sure lighting knows

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.330
how to light this.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:58.530
Boom, where are the cameras?

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.130
Okay let's look at this camera

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:01.420
and then do this.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:04.910
We're always thinking of every
single piece of the puzzle.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.390
So just to see that her mind

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:10.680
understands every part of
putting a show together

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.830
and she remembers and

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.700
she knows all of her marks

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.360
and she knows all of her lyrics

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:18.650
and how she's gonna sing everything.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:21.460
She's really in there getting it,

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:22.360
asking questions.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.223
You doing it a hundred times.

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:28.010
So we spend a lot of
time in the dance studio

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:30.050
making sure that these things come off

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:32.333
feeling like nothing.

